Requirements:
- Accepts raw file bytes.
- Exactly one `PUBLIC KEY` block: `-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----` and `-----END PUBLIC KEY-----`, each on its own line.
- Body: standard Base64, one or more lines, LF or CRLF line endings; after END marker, allow no newline or exactly one newline.
- Body: no empty lines, no spaces/tabs within lines; nothing before BEGIN or after END (including a second block).
- Base64 padding must be canonical, unused trailing bits must be zero; illegal chars, missing/extra padding, chars after padding → Malformed.
- Other labels (private key, certificate) not accepted; no guessing raw keys or hex.
- PEM marker/body corruption, and DER truncation/length mismatch/extra bytes → ImportPublicKeyError::Malformed (typed error identifiable by caller).
- Well-formed outer PEM + valid DER but algorithm Ed448/X25519 → UnsupportedAlgorithm with actual OID. DER corrupt → Malformed.
- DER entry stays DER-only, rejects PEM.
